  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The standard equation of electromagnetic wave&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>sin</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo></math>represents the direction of propagation wave.</p>On comparing the given equation with the standard&nbsp;equation, the direction of propagation is along line <math><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>z</mi></math> . Thus, unit vector along the direction of propagation is,<br /><math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math>",
